en: { 'x.end': 'This move ends the game. Count the captures and where the seeds left will go before you finish it.', 'c.cap': 'Capture', 'b.cap': 'Capture', 'x.cap': 'Capture {c} seeds with your last seed. Check which captures the opponent will have afterwards.', 'x.defend': 'Stop the capture the opponent is aiming at: change the count of the threatened pit, or sow it away first.', 'x.setup': 'Set up a capture for your next turn. If the opponent defends it misses, so weigh it against other gains.', 'tt.cap': 'Pit {p} captures {c} seeds', 'tt.defend': 'Pit {p} stops a capture', 'tt.setup': 'Pit {p} sets up a capture', 'tip.def': '💡 Tip: before sowing, check whether the opponent can capture something next.', 'tp.threat': 'Next the opponent can play pit {x} and capture {n} seeds, starting at pit {y}. Change that pit\'s count or move it first.', 'tp.capNow': 'Pit {x} captures {n} seeds, starting at pit {y}. Compare what the opponent can hit back with.', 'tp.count': '{n} seeds are left on the board. You need {w} to win — {x} more.', 'tp.hoard': 'Pit {p} holds {n} seeds. A big pile goes round and drops seeds all along the opponent\'s row, but it is also a target.', 'tp.winning': 'You are ahead. Don\'t chase captures; play safe moves that give the opponent nothing to take.', 'tp.losing': 'You are behind. Look for a big capture, or for where the seeds go at the end.', 'tp.open1': 'Early on, avoid giving captures: after your move, check where the opponent\'s last seed can stop.', 'tp.open2': 'After each move, check whether the opponent can capture something next.', 'tp.mid1': 'Don\'t leave pits on your row that are one seed short of the capture condition.', 'tp.end2': 'With few seeds left, count where the remaining seeds go when the game ends.' },
